(For a knocked-out adult tooth, tell the caller to hold it by the crown, not the root, and) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 721 Tm
(to keep it in milk if milk is nearby. Do not scrub the tooth. If the clinic is open, ask) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 706 Tm
(them to come in the same day.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 685 Tm
(The receptionist cannot promise antibiotics or pain medicine. The dentist decides that at) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 670 Tm
(the visit. A caller may use an over-the-counter pain reliever they already take, following) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 655 Tm
(the package, until they are seen. Do not give a dose.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 626 Tm
(What to bring) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 603 Tm
(Bring photo identification, a health card, an insurance card, a list of medicines, and the) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 588 Tm
(family doctor's name if they have one. A parent or guardian comes with a child under 16.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 573 Tm
(X-rays from another office can be sent ahead, but they are not required to book.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 544 Tm
(Children and pregnancy) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 521 Tm
(Dr. Amrit Bhandal is the usual dentist for children. The first child visit can be a short) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 506 Tm
(look around the clinic. Routine visits start around age one, or when the first tooth) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 491 Tm
(appears. A parent stays with the child for the exam.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 470 Tm
(Routine exams and cleanings are welcome during pregnancy. X-rays are postponed unless the) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 455 Tm
(dentist says they are needed. Ask the patient to mention the pregnancy when booking.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 426 Tm
(Whitening, crowns, and implants) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 403 Tm
(Whitening is not done on the same day as a new-patient exam. The dentist checks the gums) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 388 Tm
(first. Take-home whitening is $399 and in-office whitening is $550.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 367 Tm
(A crown is usually two visits about two weeks apart. A temporary crown should not be used) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 352 Tm
(on hard food. Implant consultations with Dr. Sarah Chen have no consultation fee.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 337 Tm
(Treatment is quoted after the exam and any x-rays.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 308 Tm
(After a visit) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 285 Tm
(After a cleaning, the gums can feel tender for a day. Brush gently that evening. Ask the) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 270 Tm
(patient to call if bleeding continues past the next day or if pain is worse after two) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 255 Tm
(days.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 234 Tm
(After an extraction, bite on the gauze for about 30 minutes. Avoid rinsing, spitting, and) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 219 Tm
(straws on that day. Soft food is fine. Avoid smoking and alcohol for 48 hours. A little) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 204 Tm
(oozing is expected. Ask the patient to call the clinic, or to seek urgent care, if) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 189 Tm
(bleeding is heavy, swelling increases after three days, or they feel unwell.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 160 Tm
(Records) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 137 Tm
